test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T19:43:43.8384507Z             "body": "This draft preserves original local stdio MCP and adds bounded batch/jobs, private profiles/artifacts, production packaging, lifecycle controls and fork-specific installation. Publishing remains disabled; release acceptance is blocked.\n\nCurrent candidate fdd83e0 archives native94 and adds a test-only bounded observer of the first eight JPEG frame headers entering each recording encoder. It forwards actual stdin writes with original arguments, callback and return value; no frames are skipped, rewritten or warmed up. No production encoder, timeout, transport-default or ownership policy changes.\n\nValidation: original strict video cases pass Chromium/Firefox on Node20/22/24 (six passes), with48 observed320x240 JPEG headers. Typecheck/lint/actionlint pass (shellcheck/pyflakes disabled);297-file dry package excludes tests and evidence. Native input geometry evidence is pending. Existing fixture retention/close-error guards and stock PCM/PNG references now pass all five native installed-package steps.\n\nLatest completed native94 at3a5b901: batch39833354256 reports1621 passes/7 failures; original39833354270 reports599/9; completed summaries2220/16. All17 logs resolved after one first empty-error read and ordinary retry. Components all pass, including12 actual concurrent schema races. All five package checks pass; this does not repair prior unconfirmed exits. Actual Codex1k passes all3 OSs, model0/owned0. Linux main207/211/211 passes; Mac206/5 and Windows201/2 remain failed.\n\nMac raw1k times out968, SDK jobs/sync fail, allowed-origin positive control times out and frozen-page cleanup fails. Windows HTTP Firefox records401 but times out, then teardown observes one scoped process with matching captured birth. Full same-snapshot legacy/root rows retained. Later127 legacy-only candidates are retained without role/name/age/window filtering. Firefox POST cancellation fails ownership confirmation before requests. No hints-based signals, unsafe replay, lease clearance or historical136/142 birth-gap clearance.\n\nOriginal main Linux200/0 Mac199/1 Windows197/3 includes eight additive stock references each. All12 stock single-PNG captures pass; stock PCM11/12, with Windows WebKit ready0 after preload and real play click. Original WebKit PCM/VP9 also fail. Mac Chromium video is gray at100,100 and319,239 in both browser and independent ffmpeg frame zero, despite red source PNG. Metadata copies retain encoded bytes and remain gray. Three fresh controls1/2 include capture and AbortError failures; fresh red samples do not repair original failure. Actual input JPEG geometry is not known from native94. Windows legacy server/headed fail actions; direct-pipe completes23/23 but fails context cleanup. Docker2/0.\n\nFull evidence and G00–G18 scopes: docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md and docs/evidence/native94-summary.json. G18 BLOCKED. No merge or publication.",
